#: title/pc5_web_page.html:142 title/pc5_web_page.html:168
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Saving…"
msgstr "Enregistrement…"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:146
msgctxt "web"
msgid ""
"Saved: its cover, background and details are fetched again when PC5 opens."
msgstr ""
"Enregistré : sa pochette, son arrière-plan et ses détails seront récupérés "
"de nouveau à l'ouverture de PC5."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:147
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Cleared: PC5 reads the game's folder again."
msgstr "Effacé : PC5 relit le dossier du jeu."

#. Web page text.
#. %s and %d are filled in by the page; %1$s, %2$s put them in another order.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:149 title/pc5_web_page.html:174
#, c-format
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Not saved: %s"
msgstr "Non enregistré : %s"

#. Web page text.
#. %s and %d are filled in by the page; %1$s, %2$s put them in another order.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:152
#, c-format
msgctxt "web"
msgid "; GOG product %s"
msgstr "; produit GOG %s"

#. Web page text.
#. %s and %d are filled in by the page; %1$s, %2$s put them in another order.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:153
#, c-format
msgctxt "web"
msgid ""
"PC5 picks the game's cover, background and details by this number (%s%s). "
"If they are another game's, type the number from the game's Steam store "
"link (store.steampowered.com/app/<number>). Empty: PC5 reads the folder "
"again."
msgstr ""
"PC5 choisit la pochette, l'arrière-plan et les détails du jeu d'après ce "
"numéro (%s%s). S'ils sont ceux d'un autre jeu, saisissez le numéro tiré du "
"lien de la page Steam du jeu (store.steampowered.com/app/<numéro>). Vide : "
"PC5 relit le dossier."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:172
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Saved: used at the game's next start."
msgstr "Enregistré : utilisé au prochain démarrage du jeu."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:187
msgctxt "web"
msgid "No games yet."
msgstr "Aucun jeu pour l'instant."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:190
msgctxt "web"
msgid "USB drive"
msgstr "Disque USB"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:191
msgctxt "web"
msgid "can't start"
msgstr "ne peut pas démarrer"

#. Web page text.
#. %s and %d are filled in by the page; %1$s, %2$s put them in another order.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:196
#, c-format
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Settings: %s"
msgstr "Paramètres : %s"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:199
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Newest log"
msgstr "Journal le plus récent"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:201
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Report a problem"
msgstr "Signaler un problème"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:202
msgctxt "web"
msgid ""
"Downloads the newest log and opens GitHub's form, filled in: attach the "
"log there."
msgstr ""
"Télécharge le journal le plus récent et ouvre le formulaire de GitHub, "
"déjà rempli : joignez-y le journal."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:208
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Launch options (launch.txt)"
msgstr "Options de lancement (launch.txt)"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:209
msgctxt "web"
msgid ""
"The first line that isn't empty or a comment (# or ;) is added to the "
"program's command line."
msgstr ""
"La première ligne qui n'est ni vide ni un commentaire (# ou ;) est ajoutée "
"à la ligne de commande du programme."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:212
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Environment variables (env.txt)"
msgstr "Variables d'environnement (env.txt)"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:212
msgctxt "web"
msgid "One NAME=value a line, set before the game starts."
msgstr "Un NOM=valeur par ligne, défini avant le démarrage du jeu."

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:213
msgctxt "web"
msgid "Extra logging (winedebug.txt)"
msgstr "Journalisation détaillée (winedebug.txt)"

#. Web page text.
#: title/pc5_web_page.html:214
msgctxt "web"
msgid ""
"Only when an issue asks for it, for example err+all,+seh. Empty it "
"afterwards: it slows the game down."
msgstr ""
"Seulement quand un ticket le demande, par exemple err+all,+seh. Videz-le "
"ensuite : il ralentit le jeu."

#. Web page text.
#. %s and %d are filled in by the page; %1$s, %2$s put them in another order.
